{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795224,"nonce":"7QcECxoZBzhXjpqSym/EDwN0ieY=","title":"Compose consented collaborator media for public OBS broadcasts","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P3\n\nScope\nBuild a restricted broadcast page/compositor for OBS that subscribes only to explicitly approved microphone/camera/screen tracks. Add host preview/layout/names and separate private-call versus public-output routing. Use scoped revocable access, never editor invitations, reusable account tokens or SFU app secrets in OBS URLs. Handle consent withdrawal, host replacement and output disconnect by closing actual subscriptions. Treat recording and per-destination publication as explicit states.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nTests prove that joining a call does not publish someone publicly, revocation stops delivery, audience cannot obtain edit access, and local/private audio is not captured twice or looped. Layout changes and guest reconnect do not retain old decoders/tracks. OBS can render the approved composition on each claimed platform, and compositor media is attributed to the room's usage owner.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}